{"id":"5d23dd05c93b7f1d4cc21d849421324fe37b38f8d52fec0a6635c59723d4dd6f","pubkey":"ec42c765418b3db9c85abff3a88f4a3bbe57535eebbdc54522041fa5328c0600","created_at":1782200549,"content":"🪪 My Nostr License — ロクヨウ\n#NostrLicense\nhttps://kojira.github.io/nostr-license/\nhttps://share.yabu.me/ec42c765418b3db9c85abff3a88f4a3bbe57535eebbdc54522041fa5328c0600/65d87ce868784b72764f064b11488b5c300dbca64a996ba21a1894a392e7a354.webp","tags":[["t","nostrlicense"],["imeta","url https://share.yabu.me/ec42c765418b3db9c85abff3a88f4a3bbe57535eebbdc54522041fa5328c0600/65d87ce868784b72764f064b11488b5c300dbca64a996ba21a1894a392e7a354.webp","m image/png","x 65d87ce868784b72764f064b11488b5c300dbca64a996ba21a1894a392e7a354","ox 65d87ce868784b72764f064b11488b5c300dbca64a996ba21a1894a392e7a354","dim 1568x2000","blurhash ULOgQotToNx[R;o3agR%?dogt6R*?wjbV@bc"]]}
{"id":"3784e48d4b8f449be90f399b93abf85132210e3cd72d2b2e5edd1874dff27543","pubkey":"c70b89f075cc6e011164cc68d3257a39253aca7409196e1a7690b66bd963ea74","created_at":1782200316,"content":"\"Why Indian Railways Runs on a Caste System: The Hidden Apartheid of Vande Bharat vs. General Coaches\"\n\nhttps://blossom.primal.net/ee817a71f960a9b275182088bc737f15250cbe1a59119e4d6f690750d59d49fe.png\n\r\n•\tIndian Railways Caste System: How Vande Bharat Excludes the Common Man\r\n•\tThe shocking truth behind India’s train apartheid where Vande Bharat’s luxury contrasts with the filth of general coaches. A system designed for the elite, not the people.\r\nSummary\r\nIndian Railways operates on a de facto caste system where the elite ride in Vande Bharat’s gleaming AC coaches while the common man is trapped in overcrowded, unsanitary general compartments. This isn’t just poor infrastructure; it’s a systemic failure of governance, where policy incentives favor the wealthy over the masses. The Public Accounts Committee (PAC) and CAG reports expose this apartheid, but the real question is: Why does India’s lifeline still run on exclusion?\r\n________________________________________\r\n\"A train journey shouldn’t feel like a social hierarchy. Yet in India, your coach class determines your dignity. The Vande Bharat vs. general coach divide isn’t just about luxury it’s about who India’s railways truly serve. And the answer is terrifying.\"\r\n________________________________________\r\nOpening\r\n\"Gandhi fought for third-class dignity. Today, India’s railways have turned his protest into a caste system where the rich ride in air-conditioned purity, and the poor choke in filth.\"\r\nContext & Problem\r\nIndian Railways carries 1.75 crore passengers daily yet only a fraction experience the sterile luxury of Vande Bharat. The rest endure:\r\n•\tOvercrowded general coaches (where 120 passengers cram into 72-seat capacity).\r\n•\tToilets so filthy that officials admit they’re \"unusable\" in long-distance trains.\r\n•\tA sanitation crisis so severe that the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) flagged it in 2023.\r\nYet the Public Accounts Committee (PAC) including a BJP member has called this out as \"casteism in disguise.\" The question isn’t just about cleanliness; it’s about who India’s railways were built for.\r\nFirst Principles Breakdown\r\nWhat people assume:\r\n•\t\"Railways are struggling financially luxury trains like Vande Bharat are a revenue necessity.\"\r\n•\t\"General coaches are ‘budget-friendly’ people choose them.\"\r\nWhat’s actually true:\r\n•\tVande Bharat’s ticket prices are higher than short-haul flights making them exclusive by design.\r\n•\tGeneral coaches are overcrowded because premium trains siphon off capacity, leaving the poor with worse service.\r\n•\tThe real cost? 1.75 crore Indians most of them not elite are forced into subhuman conditions.\r\nSystems Thinking Analysis\r\nFeedback Loops:\r\n•\tElite Bias Reinforcement: The more Vande Bharat succeeds, the more railways prioritize it, starving general coaches of investment.\r\n•\tPublic Perception Distortion: People aspire to Vande Bharat (due to marketing), normalizing the deprivation of general coaches.\r\nIncentives:\r\n•\tRailway Board’s KPIs reward profit from premium trains, not service for the masses.\r\n•\tPolitical pressure comes from elite voters, not the 1.75 crore daily passengers.\r\nLeverage Points:\r\n•\tRevenue redistribution (tax Vande Bharat profits to fund general coach upgrades).\r\n•\tMandate quotas (reserve 30% of premium train seats for general passengers).\r\n5. Design Thinking Application\r\nHuman Needs Misunderstood:\r\n•\tGeneral coach passengers don’t just need seats they need dignity.\r\n•\tToilets aren’t just facilities they’re a human right.\r\nThe 5 Profound Insights\r\n1.\t\"Casteism didn’t disappear it evolved into classism.\"\r\n•\tImplication: The poor today face the same exclusion as lower castes historically did.\r\n2.\t\"Vande Bharat isn’t a train it’s a status symbol.\"\r\n•\tImplication: The real scandal isn’t the train’s quality, but who it excludes.\r\n3.\t\"The PAC’s outrage is performative where’s the action?\"\r\n•\tImplication: Political theater without policy change is complicity.\r\n4.\t\"Gandhi’s third-class protest was about dignity today’s general coach is worse.\"\r\n•\tImplication: Progress is regression if we repeat history’s mistakes.\r\n5.\t\"The solution isn’t more trains it’s fair trains.\"\r\n•\tImplication: Quantity over quality is false efficiency.\r\n7. New Solution Model\r\nThe \"Dignity Quota\" Framework:\r\n1.\tMandate 30% general-coach seats in premium trains (Vande Bharat, Rajdhani).\r\n2.\tTax Vande Bharat’s profits to fund general coach upgrades.\r\n3.\tPublish real-time cleanliness ratings for every train (like flight reviews).\r\n4.\tMake railway officials ride general coaches for a week no exemptions.\r\n8. Step-by-Step Guide\r\n1.\tAwareness: Share CAG/PAC reports on social media.\r\n2.\tDiagnosis: Track which trains have the worst sanitation.\r\n3.\tReframing: Demand \"Dignity Quotas\" in Parliament.\r\n4.\tIntervention: Boycott trains with filthy general coaches.\r\n5.\tFeedback: File RTIs on railway cleanliness.\r\n6.\tIteration: Push for mandatory upgrades.\r\n7.\tScaling: Expand the model to buses, metros, and airports.\r\n9. Real-World Example\r\nWhat Failed:\r\n•\t2023 CAG Report flagged sanitation failures but no action. What Changed:\r\n•\tPAC’s questioning forced media scrutiny. What Worked:\r\n•\tSocial media campaigns (#CleanMyTrain) pressured officials. Lessons:\r\n•\tSilence = Complicity. Outrage must lead to action.\r\n10. Future Implications\r\nCost of Inaction:\r\n•\tHealth crises (disease spread in filthy trains).\r\n•\tSocial unrest (the poor will no longer tolerate exclusion).\r\nPossibility of Evolution:\r\n•\tIf railways adopt \"Dignity Quotas,\" India could lead global public transport justice.\r\n11. Conclusion\r\n\"A nation’s greatness isn’t measured by its Vande Bharats it’s measured by how it treats its general coaches. Gandhi’s third class was a protest. Today’s general coach is a **crime against humanity**. Will we fix it?\"\r\n12. Call to Action\r\nComment below:\r\n•\tHave you faced discrimination in Indian Railways?\r\n•\tTag a railway minister demand change.\r\n•\tFollow for more systemic exposes.\r\n________________________________________\r\nFAQ Section\r\n1.\tQ: Is Vande Bharat really that bad for the poor?\r\n•\tA: No it’s not about Vande Bharat itself, but how it starves general coaches of investment.\r\n2.\tQ: Why don’t railways just improve general coaches?\r\n•\tA: No political will. Premium trains generate more revenue, so elites get priority.\r\n3.\tQ: Can’t people just book Tatkal in general coaches?\r\n•\tA: Tatkal is a scam. 90% of seats go to travel agents, not common passengers.\r\n4.\tQ: Is this really casteism?\r\n•\tA: Yes. The poor today face the same exclusion as lower castes historically did.\r\n5.\tQ: What’s the fastest way to fix this?\r\n•\tA: Mandate \"Dignity Quotas\" in Parliament 30% general seats in premium trains.\r\n________________________________________\r\nSources\r\n1.\tThe Hindu: \"Why is there a caste system for trains?\"\r\n2.\tCAG Report on Indian Railways Sanitation (2023)\r\n3.\tPublic Accounts Committee (PAC) Observations\r\n4.\tIndian Railways Passenger Data (2024)","tags":[["imeta","m image/png","ox ee817a71f960a9b275182088bc737f15250cbe1a59119e4d6f690750d59d49fe","size 2587011","url https://blossom.primal.net/ee817a71f960a9b275182088bc737f15250cbe1a59119e4d6f690750d59d49fe.png","x ee817a71f960a9b275182088bc737f15250cbe1a59119e4d6f690750d59d49fe"],["t","cleanmytrain"]]}
