{"id":"6fb84830116c6a953e9473f9545d066a2a16748856f7de7263b3a83f48300652","pubkey":"314072c16fa9433e1374f62e5b02c8163946ed298a9cde3b1541513c29d19fff","created_at":1782198487,"content":"That’s a fair take, but just to get this out of the way, if it comes to this (meaning BIP-110 fails and the only solution left is a hard fork change of SHA-256), I’m not supporting that and will simply disconnect my node and sell my Bitcoin. I don’t think there’s any merit in discussing hard forks, since we know they are a non-starter. We didn’t avoid them like the plague for 17 years just to pivot now. In fact I think even discussing them at this point is eroding the case for BIP-110 and giving higher ground for the bad actors. Sorry nostr:npub1lh273a4wpkup00stw8dzqjvvrqrfdrv2v3v4t8pynuezlfe5vjnsnaa9nk and nostr:nprofile1qqs8fl79rnpsz5x00xmvkvtd8g2u7ve2k2dr3lkfadyy4v24r4k3s4spremhxue69uhkummnw3ez6ur4vgh8wetvd3hhyer9wghxuet59uq3zamnwvaz7tmwdaehgu3wwa5kuef03j9hac, but if you search deeper, you’ll see that I’m right. We better make BIP-110 successful or we’re all screwed and Bitcoin will die.\nhttps://blossom.primal.net/41a6d30eb027f793121a285c77ce8ab67301be03d249e3f7789f639233f64c47.jpg","tags":[["p","74ffc51cc30150cf79b6cb316d3a15cf332ab29a38fec9eb484ab1551d6d1856","wss://nostr-pub.wellorder.net/","mention"],["p","fdd5e8f6ae0db817be0b71da20498c1806968d8a6459559c249f322fa73464a7","","mention"],["imeta","url https://blossom.primal.net/41a6d30eb027f793121a285c77ce8ab67301be03d249e3f7789f639233f64c47.jpg","m jpeg","dim 1284.0x1461.0"]]}
